This version of xosview is distributed from the following sites:

  http://www.pogo.org.uk/~mark/xosview/
  https://github.com/hills/xosview

The source is C: C89 for the vendor Unix ports, which is all their
compilers accept, and whatever the local gcc or clang takes for Linux
and the BSDs.

The build no longer uses GNU autoconfig, and needs no GNU make either:
one Makefile holds every platform, and the vendor make will do.

  $ make
  $ make install

"make" identifies the system with uname and hands off to the matching
target.  To pick one yourself, name it:

  $ make hpux9

The targets are linux, gnu, freebsd, netbsd, openbsd, dragonflybsd,
sunos5, aix4, aix5, hpux9, hpux10, hpux11, irix5, irix65, osf1, osr6
and unixware.  Each one sets CC, CFLAGS, LDFLAGS, LIBS and the meter
objects for its platform, and any of those can be overridden on the
command line:

  $ make linux CC=clang
  $ make install PREFIX=/usr

Please see the README file for your platform for any special
instructions for running xosview on that platform.

See the man page for information on the xosview display and how to
customize it.

See the COPYING file for licensing terms.
